{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>They.</b> Now from the time they spoke to Pharaoh, Scripture places Moses first because of his great greatness, and HaShem spoke with him face to face, and he drew near to the cloud where HaShem was, and not so Aaron. And Scripture testifies: 'Not so My servant Moses' (Numbers 12:7). And Aaron said to him at times: 'Please, my lord' — therefore you will not find in all the Torah the beginning of this verse where Moses does not precede Aaron, and likewise in the Prophets, and likewise in the Writings. And there is no argument from the phrase 'These are the descendants of Aaron and Moses' (Numbers 3:1), nor from 'She bore him Aaron and Moses' (Numbers 26:59), for when they were born it mentioned them [in birth order], and the proof is 'descendants' and also 'she bore.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:14.715714923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}